hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17682","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj narrated to us, who said: I heard 'Umayr, freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, who said: I and 'Abd Allah ibn Yasar, freedman of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), approached; we entered upon Abu Juhaym ibn al-Harith ibn al-Simmah al-Ansari. Abu Juhaym said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approached from the direction of Bi'r Jamal, and a man met him and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not return his greeting until he faced the wall, wiped his face and hands, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his greeting."
"17683","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to me: Busr ibn Sa'id informed me, who said: Abu Juhaym narrated to me that two men differed about a verse of the Qur'an. One said: I received it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the other said: I received it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The Qur'an is recited in seven modes, so do not dispute about the Qur'an, for dispute about the Qur'an is disbelief."
